):**\n    The definitive source for every commit and version bump is the [MLX GitHub Repository Releases](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/releases). This will list every bug fix, new feature, and breaking change.\n2.  **MLX Documentation:**\n    For high-level guides on how to use new features, visit the [official MLX documentation](https://ml-explore.github.io/mlx/).\n3.  **PyPI / Conda:**\n    If you are looking for the version currently installed in your environment, you can run:\n    ```bash\n    pip show mlx\n    ```\n\n**Pro Tip:** If you are working with LLMs specifically, you should also monitor the **[mlx-examples](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-examples)** repository, as many of the newest model implementations and optimization techniques are released there first.", "tool_calls": [], "metrics": {"prompt_tokens": 265, "generation_tokens": 450, "prompt_tps": 1967.9, "generation_tps": 120.9, "peak_memory": 0.0, "reused_prefix": 192, "token_breakdown": {"thinking": 0, "visible": 448, "tool_json": 0, "marker_overhead": 2}}, "wall_s": 3.86}], "wall_s": 4.4, "aborted_reason": "", "score": {"parse_errors": 0, "hallucinated_tools": [], "final_ok": true, "turns_used": 2, "aborted": false, "first_shot_ok": true, "valid_call_ok": true, "corrected": false, "pass": true, "why": []}, "cot": {"turns": [{"ctrl_leaks": [], "think_chars": 0, "empty_think": true, "dup_rate": 0.0, "recite_rate": 0.0, "scripts": {"cjk": 0.0, "latin": 0.0, "other": 0.0}}, {"ctrl_leaks": [], "think_chars": 0, "empty_think": true, "dup_rate": 0.0, "recite_rate": 0.0, "scripts": {"cjk": 0.0, "latin": 0.0, "other": 0.0}}], "any_ctrl_leak": false, "max_dup_rate": 0.0, "max_recite_rate": 0.0, "max_other_script": 0.0, "empty_think_turns": 2, "think_chars_total": 0}}
